{
  "keyPoints": [
    {
      "id": "kp1",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "`max_tokens` is accepted and ignored on cli (\"the model's own output limit applies\"), whereas the sdk enforces it to the token."
    },
    {
      "id": "kp2",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "a 64-token budget can be spent entirely on thinking: the response ends with `stop_reason: max_tokens` and no text block"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp3",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "assumes block 0 is text; with a thinking block it is the wrong block, returns null, `sanitizeLabel(null)` gives `null`, and the graceful-degradation path"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp4",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "run each pinned site once live with its real prompt on the pinned model and read `stop_reason` and usage; raise caps from those measurements"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp5",
      "hit": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "kp6",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "`MAX_LABEL_CHARS` already bounds kept output, so a generous cap costs thinking tokens only."
    }
  ],
  "traps": [
    {
      "id": "trap1",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "trap2",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "trap3",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "trap4",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    }
  ],
  "decisionCorrect": {
    "value": true,
    "quote": "Do not merge yet: the sdk pin turns an ignored `max_tokens` into an enforced one"
  },
  "rationale": "The response identifies both the enforced-cap and block-index failures and prescribes the required checks and fixes. It notes the audit gap and live runs, but does not explicitly distinguish unavailable from failed."
}

