{
  "keyPoints": [
    {
      "id": "kp1",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "`isHostedSupabaseHost` was a proxy for \"not disposable\", and its docstring states the premise that made it true: exactly one Supabase project, always production. The cutover falsified that premise"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp2",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "the shared predicate should be an allowlist of loopback hosts (localhost, 127.0.0.0/8, ::1) and treat every unrecognised host as somebody's real database. That fails closed and cannot rot when the store moves again."
    },
    {
      "id": "kp3",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "Both callers stay on that single predicate."
    },
    {
      "id": "kp4",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "`testUrl === productionUrl` compares strings, and two strings name one database easily: an appended `?sslmode=`, different credentials, localhost against 127.0.0.1, an implicit port. Compare host, port and database name instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "kp5",
      "hit": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "kp6",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "production DSN with no comparison, production plus a query parameter, a loopback alias of production. Allowed before, refused after, with the container DSN still allowed so a guard that refuses everything cannot pass. Throw away the regenerated fixture and rebuild it from a fresh migration replay"
    }
  ],
  "traps": [
    {
      "id": "trap1",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "trap2",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "trap3",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "trap4",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    }
  ],
  "decisionCorrect": {
    "value": true,
    "quote": "Replace the hostname denylist with a loopback allowlist in the shared predicate, compare production by host, port and database, add no bypass, and regenerate the fixture from a fresh replay."
  },
  "rationale": "The response reaches the correct decision and covers the root cause, shared predicate, identity check, verification, and fixture regeneration. It rejects a bypass but does not specify a refusal message naming the host and safe alternative."
}

